---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FurtherReading from '../components/FurtherReading.astro';
import SeaBreak from '../components/SeaBreak.astro';
import { ocean, photos, scenes } from '../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Credentials', href: '/credentials/' }];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Credentials & Training"
  description="Mo Lumen's astrology training and professional service: STA Horary Practitioner's Certificate, NCGR-PAA Levels 1–2 examinations, Dwarf Planet University diploma and teaching, OPA board service, and 2026 United Astrology Conference staff service."
  path="/credentials/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Training & service</p>
        <h1>Credentials</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Credentials do not tell you whether an astrologer's approach will fit you, but they can
          tell you what that person has studied, where they have been tested, and how seriously they
          stay engaged with the work.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img class="hero__img" src={scenes.chartDetail.src} srcset={scenes.chartDetail.srcset} sizes="100vw" alt={scenes.chartDetail.alt} width={scenes.chartDetail.width} height={scenes.chartDetail.height} fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid grid--2" style="align-items: start;">
      <figure class="portrait-card">
        <img src={photos.moCredentials.src} alt={photos.moCredentials.alt} width={photos.moCredentials.width} height={photos.moCredentials.height} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Mo Lumen</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="prose flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Formal study</p>
        <h2>Training, certification & examination</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Practitioner's Certificate in Horary Astrology</strong>: School of Traditional Astrology (STA).</li>
          <li><strong>NCGR-PAA certification exams, Levels 1 and 2, passed</strong>; Level 3 in progress.</li>
          <li><strong>Diploma, Dwarf Planet University (DPU)</strong>; current assistant teacher and tutor at DPU.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>Why this matters in my work:</strong> structured study gives me methods to test against the chart rather than relying only on impression. Teaching and tutoring also keep asking me to explain why a technique says what I think it says, which is a useful discipline when I am sitting with a client.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Professional community</p>
      <h2>Service & memberships</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Board member &amp; treasurer</strong>: <a href="https://opaastrology.org/about-opa/meet-the-board/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Organization for Professional Astrologers (OPA)</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Treasurer</strong>: NCGR-DFW chapter, 2024–2026.</li>
        <li><strong>Bookkeeper</strong>: 2026 United Astrology Conference staff.</li>
        <li>Member: <a href="https://ncgrastrology.org/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">NCGR</a>, <a href="https://opaastrology.org/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">OPA</a>, and <a href="https://www.isarastrology.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ISAR</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Professional organizations put me in continuing conversation with astrologers who use
        different techniques and traditions. I value that because I do not want one school or one
        familiar method to become the only way I know how to look.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SeaBreak image={ocean.glassWave} />

  <section class="section section--sea">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>A wider background</h2>
      <p>
        Astrology has interested me since childhood, although I came to it professionally later.
        Along the way I taught natural sciences from middle school through college and worked in
        business and financial roles. The science classroom especially shaped how I observe,
        question, explain complex ideas, and respect the relationships between parts of a larger
        system.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>Training is only one part of choosing an astrologer.</strong> Approach tells you how that knowledge is used, how uncertainty is handled, and whether your own experience has a place in the conversation.</p>
      </div>
      <FurtherReading />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    heading="Want to know how I use what I've studied?"
    body="Credentials tell you about training. My Approach shows what that training looks like when I am actually reading a chart with another person."
    buttonLabel="Read My Approach"
    buttonHref="/approach/"
    secondaryLabel="See How Readings Work"
    secondaryHref="/how-readings-work/"
  />
</BaseLayout>
